{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"5daee24569467eed42406021f4a5d2e1bd3e4083bc5ff8f061411cb08a84ce68","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_88ab0c270cff8f391a7a4dc89bd877b4cc945f8409f663f7fc0cec290d515328","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a simple, parameter-free method (AdaBN) that leverages Batch Normalization statistics for domain adaptation. It demonstrates strong performance on standard benchmarks and a practical remote sensing application, offering a low-cost alternative to complex adaptation techniques.","paper_id":"BJuysoFeg","paper_identity_sha256":"0088bbdb2adc7d50aae589012f32b341ac8334536f418c5239836c76e90f75c9","prompt_identity_sha256":"8c94e1dadd2203cb9540285c2d132319eff5db7d57a545221c530309a75d8483","raw_response_sha256":"227e002c143f1d011e263c551223c0390c995596a031af89fe26ea7c33be1d77","request_identity_sha256":"6e80bf0f58890e1adb1e684d085e83cea837f160309e07b59e4c4271ae56db27","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"84e2a12c3295618f3864afb04999e081a7373ae7ab62fc14b0d1a3c1caaa5ccf","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-004","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The work addresses the broadly important problem of domain adaptation in deep learning, which is a significant challenge for generalizing models across different data distributions. The proposed method, Adaptive Batch Normalization (AdaBN), is notable for its simplicity and parameter-free nature, which could influence a wide range of researchers by providing a low-cost, easy-to-implement alternative to more complex adaptation techniques. The paper suggests that this approach opens a new direction for domain adaptation, potentially impacting multiple research areas that rely on transfer learning and model generalization.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-031","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates domain-specific impact through its application to cloud detection in remote sensing images, a specialized field where domain shift is a critical issue due to differences in satellite sensors and resolutions. The method shows significant improvements in mIOU on the GF1 and Tianhui datasets, indicating its practical utility in this domain. Additionally, the method's applicability to large-size segmentation tasks, where other methods may be computationally intensive, highlights its relevance for real-world applications in remote sensing.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-023","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The paper reports state-of-the-art performance on standard domain adaptation benchmarks, including Office-31 and Caltech-Bing. On the Office-31 dataset, AdaBN achieves an average accuracy of 77.2%, outperforming previous methods such as DAN (72.9%) and Deep CORAL (72.1%). In the multi-source setting, AdaBN combined with CORAL achieves an average of 84.4%, surpassing the baseline and CORAL alone. These results indicate substantial and consistent improvements over strong baselines, supporting the claim that the method advances the state of the art in domain adaptation.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The method has potential real-world impact due to its minimal computational requirements and ease of implementation, which could facilitate its adoption in practical settings where resources are limited. The paper highlights the method's value in scenarios where a large number of target images are not available, as it can achieve good results with only a small subset of target examples. However, the paper does not extensively discuss broader societal impacts, such as fairness or environmental considerations, which are not directly relevant to the technical focus of the work.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"b8687f0b46c3fe5484238b0839d90baba8176c14c00a081c60d4a3d96192a81e","paper_id":"BJuysoFeg","paper_ordinal":40,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"227e002c143f1d011e263c551223c0390c995596a031af89fe26ea7c33be1d77","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJuysoFeg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"b26e27e07a34630ca60c0fdb8e8ae50209195e5624941ac1ccfe9669054464fe","request_identity_sha256":"6e80bf0f58890e1adb1e684d085e83cea837f160309e07b59e4c4271ae56db27","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":770,"prompt_tokens":19644,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20414},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"6e80bf0f58890e1adb1e684d085e83cea837f160309e07b59e4c4271ae56db27","role":"SIGN","role_ordinal":2,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}